repository-code: "https://github.com/SequenceOfManyZerosAndOnes/RICAN"
abstract: "RICAN (Representational Isomorphic Coding for Arbitrary Numeration) is a mathematical framework for constructing asymptotically tight fixed-rate reversible binary representations for sequences over arbitrary finite alphabets. The method selects block sizes through continued-fraction approximation of log2(B), producing deterministic fixed-rate representations with rounding gaps converging to zero along suitable subsequences of convergent denominators. The framework applies uniformly to all finite alphabets, including DNA sequences, decimal digits, and byte alphabets."
